      "right": "480px",
      "width": "450px",
      "text": "<span class=\"sugya-marker sugya-marker-steinsaltz\" data-sugya-kind=\"steinsaltz\" data-sugya-id=\"466\" data-sentence-id=\"2\" data-steinsaltz-label=\"א\"></span> <span class=\"sentence\" id=\"2\" type=\"start\">&star;</span>אָמַר <span class=\"name-reference-marker name-reference-amora\" data-sage-type=\"amora\" title=\"Rav Huna (רב הונא) — second/third-generation Amora, principal disciple of Rav and head of Sura\" data-authority-id=\"895\" data-full-name=\"Rav Huna\" data-name-he=\"רַב הוּנָא א׳\" data-resolution-rule=\"toledot_rav_huna\" data-resolution-explanation=\"Identified as Rav Huna of Sura — the second/third-generation Amora and principal disciple of Rav — following Hyman&#x27;s Toledot Tannaim veAmoraim.\" data-resolution-reasons=\"[{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;scholarly_source&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Toledot Tannaim veAmoraim witness&quot;,&quot;detail&quot;:&quot;Hyman ties this daf to Rav Huna — the second/third-generation Amora, principal disciple of Rav, who succeeded to the chair of Sura; the famous Rav Huna whose rulings pervade the Bavli.&quot;,&quot;attribution&quot;:&quot;Hyman, Toledot Tannaim veAmoraim, s.v. רב הונא&quot;},{&quot;type&quot;:&quot;scholarly_source&quot;,&quot;label&quot;:&quot;Setam-Rav-Huna principle&quot;,&quot;detail&quot;:&quot;Rashi (Yevamot 83b) and Hyman rule that a plain, unqualified «רב הונא» is certainly the famous Rav Huna of Sura — «אבל היכי דאתמר סתמא ודאי הוא ר\\&quot;ה». No later or patronymic qualifier is present here.&quot;,&quot;attribution&quot;:&quot;Rashi, Yevamot 83b s.v. אמרי בי רב (with Hyman, s.v. רב הונא)&quot;}]\">רַב הוּנָא</span><span class=\"ein_mishpat_marker\" data-ein-mishpat-id=\"3\" data-marker-letter=\"ד\">ד</span>: שְׁכִיב מְרַע שֶׁכָּתַב כׇּל נְכָסָיו לְאַחֵר –",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
    },
    {
      "right": "480px",
      "width": "450px",
      "text": "רוֹאִין; אִם רָאוּי לְיוֹרְשׁוֹ – נוֹטְלָן מִשּׁוּם יְרוּשָּׁה, וְאִם לָאו –",
      "segment_ids": [
        2
      ]
